    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 43 Raymond Street is a superb terraced Victorian villa-style home ideally located just off the South Circular Road, one of central Dublin's most sought-after residential locations and only a short distance from the city centre and St. Stephen's Green.\n\nThe home is approached from a granite step that leads into to a fine front door with fan light above. Inside the home you are met by an impressive hallway with original timber floorboards, open fire place, sash windows and high ceilings. Moving downstairs, from the hallway to the garden floor where the hallway at this level includes a large understairs storage area. There is one bedroom and a kitchen/ dining room. This open plan room is the heart of the home and boasts a wooden framed fireplace with shelving and access to the kitchen with floor and wall mounted shelving with the bathroom to the rear. Finally, the upstairs level of the home host 2 large double bedrooms with original timber floor and rear garden views. \nThe rear garden is a special feature of this city home. It is low maintenance, landscaped and not overlooked to the rear.\n\nSuperbly located in this fashionable and sought-after district on the doorstep of the heart of the city. All social and essential amenities are close by to include Griffith College and some of the south city centre's most trendy eateries and coffee houses including Noshington, Scéal, Bastible, Gaillot et Gray and Bibi's to name but a few. Transport is well catered for making the car a luxury not a necessity, however two resident parking permits are available to request from Dublin City Council."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.40m x 1.50m\nWelcoming entrance hall with high ceilings and access to the bight living room.\n\nLiving Room - 4.65m x 4.15m\nHigh ceiling, open plan timber frame fireplace, picture rail, timber flooring, and large sash windows to the front.\n\nDining Room - 5.01m x 3.00m\nBright and spacious room with open fire with a timber frame, light filled room with kitchen access to the rear.\n\nKitchen - 3.00m x 1.55m\nTiled kitchen, with floor storage, plumbed for a washing machine/dishwasher, with the bathroom to the rear and access to the large back garden\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.00m x 2.95m\nTimber flooring, spacious double bedroom with a large window filling the room with natural light and rear garden views.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.90m x 2.70m\nTimber flooring, single bedroom with a large window filling the room with natural light and rear garden views.\n\nBedroom 3/ Study - \nLocated downstairs with connecting door to the kitchen and a view of the rear garden.\n\nBathroom - 3.90m x 2.70m\nTiled bathroom, WC, whb located off the kitchen.\n\n"
      },
